            <ArticleTitle>Left main coronary artery spasm following percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>161-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with reversible spasm of the left main coronary artery occurring shortly after successful angioplasty of a mid-LAD lesion is reported. Prompt recognition of this rare entity may be life-saving.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
